					"s4"
				],
				"technique": [
					"slice"
				]
			}
		],
		"notes": {
			"techniques": "A dry cure of equal parts salt and sugar for 48 hours, then thin slicing at a sharp angle off the skin.",
			"chemistry": "Salt draws out water by osmosis and denatures the surface proteins, firming the fish; sugar balances the salt and keeps the texture supple. Mustard acts as the emulsifier in the sauce.",
